  "description": "Deploy one Dataverse solution to a whole group of environments at once. Pick a source environment and a solution, pick a saved group of targets, and install, update, upgrade or delete it across all of them as managed or unmanaged - with a pre-flight check against every target that surfaces missing dependencies and validation failures before anything is written. Groups are named subsets of your own XrmToolBox connections, so a group is set up once and reused. To remove managed solutions, queue them up and let the tool work out the order from Dataverse's own dependency data - pulling in anything else that has to go - then delete them one at a time, top to bottom, in every environment you tick. When a single solution refuses to uninstall, it traces every blocking dependency and every unmanaged layer, tells you which solution owns each blocker, and builds an ordered removal plan it will execute for you a step at a time, with a typed confirmation on every destructive step. Read the solution.xml of any package without leaving the tool. You need the System Customizer role (or System Administrator) on a licensed account - System Customizer carries the customization privileges this uses.",
